  "_comment": "OpenLAV (Open Library of Affective Videos) clips, replacing the earlier FilmStim set (see project memory for that history). assets/clips is now a junction to D:\\Datasets\\OpenLAV (was D:\\videos). category->valence_group: joy/satisfaction/fascination -> positive, anxiety/fear/sadness -> negative, indifference -> neutral. disgust was intentionally dropped from negative per explicit user request (2026-07-30). surprise/compassion/irritation/rage excluded (ambiguous valence or too few clips -- see build script comments). Every clip here is language_free=TRUE per the dataset's own metadata (no spoken dialogue/narration), so there is no language-bias concern at all this time, unlike the FilmStim French-clips issue. Manifest deliberately includes the FULL language_free pool per mapped category (not a hand-picked subset) so run_emotion_task's existing per-session random group_clips shuffle draws from real variety -- every participant should see a different set of clips, not the same ~8 recycled each time. 2026-08-11: clip_82-84 (filmstim_positive) / clip_85-87 (filmstim_negative) are a hand-picked, participant-supplied set of 3 positive + 3 negative clips (own files, not from OpenLAV) that fully REPLACE OpenLAV for those two valence groups this session -- see app/config/emotion_fixed_clips.json and emotion_task.clips_per_group in session_config.yaml (now {positive: 3, negative: 3, neutral: 4}). Neutral is untouched and still drawn from OpenLAV.",
